{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"a29d5859530e551c9c63051e6b73ecbf9e195803"},"timestamp":1576026734,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1MzYwODI5Nzg=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3916","origin":"github"},"title":"\"datalad status\" no terminal output for clean datasets","message":"#### What is the problem?\n`datalad status` shows no response on dataset without changes.\n\n#### What steps will reproduce the problem?\n`datalad save ; datalad status`\n\n#### What version of DataLad are you using (run `datalad --version`)? On what operating system (consider running `datalad wtf`)?\n`datalad 0.12.0rc6`\n\n#### Is there anything else that would be useful to know in this context?\nThis is no bug. If there is nothing to stage or commit, `datalad status` does not return anything, no message at all. This is a bit confusing, it would make sense to actually return something on the terminal, maybe \"nothing to save\" etc, similar to what `git status` returns when there is nothing to commit.\n\n#### Have you had any success using DataLad before? (to assess your expertise/prior luck.  We would welcome your testimonial additions to https://github.com/datalad/datalad/wiki/Testimonials as well)\nN/A","files":null}]}